+ *                every such value is exact;
+ *   reduction:   two such words, |sum| <= 4 on a 1/32 grid; bf16's step AT 4 is exactly 1/32,
+ *                so the sum is exact at every magnitude reached;
+ *   messages:    |y| <= 8 on a 1/8 grid, |sum| <= 16, exactly bf16 at every magnitude reached.
+ *
+ * Every partial sum is exact in fp32 as well, so an fma or a reassociation cannot move a byte.
+ * The WRITE is where a rounding mode is exercised: h is a half-integer up to 64 and the gain
